[/TABLE]

Again, several points worth noting:

[LIST=1]
[*]The exact solve's 100% is definitional — it hits the target, so both metrics go to zero.
[*]Look instead at the exact solve's raw column: those countries were already 19% to 20% off on mean deviation, with the worst stratum 39% to 56% off. Countries where the exact solve is feasible are not "already roughly correct"; they are just as far off, they simply happen to land inside the cone.
[*]The approximation is the real body of cases, 236 to 407 countries. L1 improves 43% to 67%, bringing mean deviation from around 30% down to roughly 10%; Linf improves about 50%, bringing the worst stratum from 69% off down to 35%.
[/LIST]

[B]4.3 Prefilter effect[/B]

The size filter blocks a lot of countries. What does it cost and what does it buy?

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Item[/TH][TH]1337.10[/TH][TH]1386.03[/TH][TH]1743.04[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]countries filtered[/TD][TD]965 (67.0%)[/TD][TD]629 (59.4%)[/TD][TD]261 (44.3%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]location traversal given up[/TD][TD]1,751 (13.1%)[/TD][TD]1,176 (8.7%)[/TD][TD]521 (2.7%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]of which exactly solvable[/TD][TD]0 (0.0%)[/TD][TD]2 (0.3%)[/TD][TD]0 (0.0%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]of which approximable[/TD][TD]565 (58.5%)[/TD][TD]390 (62.0%)[/TD][TD]113 (43.3%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]of which unsolvable anyway[/TD][TD]400 (41.5%)[/TD][TD]237 (37.7%)[/TD][TD]148 (56.7%)[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

The benefit is clear: it blocks 40% to 70% of countries while giving up only 2.7% to 13.1% of location traversal, with little impact on population demand balance.

The cost needs separating out. [B]Almost no exact solves are sacrificed[/B], which matches expectation: below four locations the matrix has at most 3 non-empty columns and cannot cover four strata. What is actually given up is approximation opportunity — 43% to 62% of the filtered countries could have received an approximate solution.

This is a performance decision. Adding the prefilter costs little while cutting sweep triggers substantially. In measurement, only with the prefilter in place does monthly computation reach an imperceptible level.

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]5. Performance[/B][/SIZE]

The unit of measure is variable operations ([ICODE]set_variable[/ICODE] / [ICODE]change_variable[/ICODE]), the dominant cost in Jomini script.

[B]5.1 Unit costs[/B]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Stage[/TH][TH]Cost[/TH][TH]Detail[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]raw stage, per location[/TD][TD]70[/TD][TD]five strata's income, spending, savings pressure, raw coefficient[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]classify + matrix aggregation, per location[/TD][TD]37[/TD][TD]share scoring, clipping, confidence, column accumulation[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]solver setup, per country[/TD][TD]120[/TD][TD]variable resets, target and baseline sums, capacity split[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]exact solve (4x4)[/TD][TD]112[/TD][TD]Gaussian elimination + back substitution + nonnegativity check[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]one vertex case[/TD][TD]218[/TD][TD]elimination + back substitution + two metrics + accept test[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]full vertex sweep (209 cases)[/TD][TD]45,562[/TD][TD]previous row x 209[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

One sweep costs 45,562 against the exact solve's 112 — a factor of 407. So the performance bottleneck is simply how many countries fall through into the sweep (the approximate path).

Recall the data from 4.1: nearly all countries that enter the solver do. That is precisely why the prefilter exists.

[B]5.2 Monthly totals[/B]

The figures below use section 4's measured path distribution — sweep counts are the countries that actually reach a sweep, not an estimate from the feasibility upper bound. Listed per timepoint:

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Configuration[/TH][TH]1337.10[/TH][TH]1386.03[/TH][TH]1743.04[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]all on + prefilter[/TD][TD]22,520,315[/TD][TD]19,498,487[/TD][TD]16,635,780[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]default (prefilter + AI reduced frequency)[/TD][TD]2,744,997 (12.2%)[/TD][TD]2,507,632 (12.9%)[/TD][TD]2,663,573 (16.0%)[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

The prefilter's benefit was given in 4.3: it trades a small amount of traversal for most of the sweep triggers.

AI frequency reduction saves a further 84% to 88%. In single player there is one human country and the rest are AI, whose solving moves to their own anniversary pulse, so only about 1/12 of them solve in any given month. The raw stage and the modifier writes are not reduced — they run every month regardless — so what is saved is the solving portion, and that portion was over 90% of the total to begin with.

1743's reduction benefit is slightly lower (84.0% versus 87.8%) because it has the most locations, and since the raw stage is unaffected by frequency reduction it takes a larger share of the total.

Worth noting that the three timepoints' totals are fairly close (16.6M to 22.5M) even though the country count falls from 1,441 to 589. The reason is that later countries are larger: total locations actually rise from 13,318 to 19,535 while sweep counts fall from 462 to 318, and the two roughly cancel.

[B]5.3 Cost distribution[/B]

Under all-on + prefilter (1337.10):

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Stage[/TH][TH]Monthly operations[/TH][TH]Share[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]raw location traversal[/TD][TD]932,260[/TD][TD]4.1%[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]classify + matrix aggregation[/TD][TD]427,979[/TD][TD]1.9%[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]solver setup[/TD][TD]57,120[/TD][TD]0.3%[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]exact solve[/TD][TD]53,312[/TD][TD]0.2%[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]vertex sweep[/TD][TD]21,049,644[/TD][TD]93.5%[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]total[/B][/TD][TD][B]22,520,315[/B][/TD][TD][B]100%[/B][/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]6. Conclusion[/B][/SIZE]

This system demonstrates one thing: even with a severely constrained engine API, appropriate mathematical modelling can still recover the information.

The measured outcome: 29.2% to 41.8% of countries receive a correction, and for those the approximation improves mean relative deviation by up to 70% and worst-stratum deviation by 50%.

The exact solve, although the preferred path, accounts for only 1.0% to 3.3% of real cases.

Performance holds up too: the default configuration runs 2.5M to 2.7M variable operations per save-month. In testing, players notice essentially no delay.
